{
 "_comment": "Phase 4 registry of repos the Schemathesis contract fuzz (qa/contract_fuzz.py) can run on, besides the in-code iptv_apps entry. Same schema as contract_fuzz.REPOS (clone, app_dir, venv_python[], app, openapi_path, env{} NON-SECRET placeholders ({tmp} = per-run temp dir), auth{register,login}, exclude_paths[[regex, reason]], optional auth_loss_max). An entry missing a required key is ignored (the repo then reports NA). Adding a repo = add an entry here, then follow qa/contract_fuzz.README.md 'Onboarding a repo' (manual first run, triage, --accept-baseline, then add it to OVN_FUZZ_REPOS in the cron). Rule for exclude_paths: any route that can open a socket to anything but the app's own DB is excluded, with the reason. Entries below were written from the repos' route tables and Settings classes (billwatch: app imports and serves 148 paths with exactly this env on the Mac, 2026-10-17); a FIRST RUN on the box is still required before the baseline.",
 "billwatch": {
  "clone": "billwatch",
  "app_dir": "billwatch-backend",
  "venv_python": [
   ".venv/bin/python",
   "venv/bin/python"
  ],
  "app": "app.main:app",
  "openapi_path": "/openapi.json",
  "env": {
   "DATABASE_URL": "sqlite+aiosqlite:///{tmp}/fuzz.db",
   "ENVIRONMENT": "development",
   "SECRET_KEY": "contract-fuzz-dummy-secret-key-0123456789abcdef",
   "CONGRESS_API_KEY": "",
   "OPEN_STATES_API_KEY": "",
   "FEC_API_KEY": "",
   "GOOGLE_CIVIC_API_KEY": "",
   "FIREBASE_CREDENTIALS_PATH": "",
   "FIREBASE_CREDENTIALS_JSON": "",
   "SMTP_USER": "",
   "SMTP_PASSWORD": "",
   "SENDGRID_API_KEY": "",
   "STRIPE_SECRET_KEY": "",
   "STRIPE_PUBLISHABLE_KEY": "",
   "STRIPE_WEBHOOK_SECRET": "",
   "STRIPE_PREMIUM_PRICE_ID": "",
   "ANTHROPIC_API_KEY": "",
   "SENTRY_DSN": ""
  },
  "auth": {
   "register": {
    "path": "/api/auth/register",
    "json": {
     "email": "contract-fuzz@example.com",
     "password": "Fuzz!Pass-123456",
     "display_name": "contract fuzz"
    }
   },
   "login": {
    "path": "/api/auth/login",
    "form": {
     "username": "contract-fuzz@example.com",
     "password": "Fuzz!Pass-123456"
    },
    "token_field": "access_token"
   }
  },
  "exclude_paths": [
   [
    "^/api/bills/sync",
    "pulls bills / sponsors from congress.gov"
   ],
   [
    "^/api/legislators/sync",
    "pulls legislators / stats from congress.gov"
   ],
   [
    "^/api/civic/",
    "Google Civic API"
   ],
   [
    "^/api/finance/",
    "OpenFEC API"
   ],
   [
    "^/api/legislators/\\{legislator_id\\}/(finance|disclosures)$",
    "OpenFEC / disclosure fetches"
   ],
   [
    "^/api/feedback$",
    "sends mail"
   ],
   [
    "^/api/auth/forgot-password$",
    "sends mail"
   ],
   [
    "^/api/billing/(checkout|portal|webhook)$",
    "Stripe API"
   ],
   [
    "^/api/analytics/summaries/generate-batch$",
    "Anthropic API"
   ],
   [
    "^/api/bills/\\{bill_id\\}/chat$",
    "Anthropic API"
   ],
   [
    "^/api/bills/\\{bill_id\\}/background$",
    "Anthropic / congress.gov background generation"
   ],
   [
    "^/api/articles/rank$",
    "fetches article URLs"
   ],
   [
    "^/api/(share-image|bills/\\{bill_id\\}/share-image)$",
    "may fetch remote images"
   ],
   [
    "^/api/export/account$",
    "deletes the throwaway user whose token the run uses"
   ]
  ]
 },
 "gitlark": {
  "clone": "gitlark",
  "app_dir": "backend",
  "venv_python": [
   ".venv/bin/python",
   "venv/bin/python"
  ],
  "app": "app.main:app",
  "openapi_path": "/openapi.json",
  "env": {
   "DATABASE_URL": "sqlite+aiosqlite:///{tmp}/fuzz.db",
   "ENVIRONMENT": "development",
   "SECRET_KEY": "contract-fuzz-dummy-secret-key-0123456789abcdef",
   "GITHUB_CLIENT_ID": "contract-fuzz-dummy-client-id",
   "GITHUB_CLIENT_SECRET": "",
   "GITHUB_WEBHOOK_SECRET": "",
   "GITHUB_WEBHOOK_TOKEN": "",
   "NOTIFICATIONS_INGEST_TOKEN": "",
   "GITHUB_APP_ENABLED": "false",
   "GITHUB_APP_ID": "",
   "GITHUB_APP_PRIVATE_KEY": "",
   "GITHUB_APP_CLIENT_ID": "",
   "GITHUB_APP_CLIENT_SECRET": "",
   "GITHUB_PAT_SHRIKE_LABS_MARK": "",
   "ANTHROPIC_API_KEY": "",
   "LOCAL_LLM_API_KEY": "",
   "STRIPE_SECRET_KEY": "",
   "STRIPE_WEBHOOK_SECRET": ""
  },
  "auth": null,
  "auth_loss_max": 1.01,
  "exclude_paths": [
   [
    "^/api/auth/github",
    "GitHub OAuth token exchange"
   ],
   [
    "^/api/github",
    "GitHub API + webhooks"
   ],
   [
    "^/api/billing",
    "Stripe API"
   ],
   [
    "^/api/connectors",
    "third-party connector calls"
   ],
   [
    "^/api/connector-credentials",
    "third-party connector calls"
   ],
   [
    "^/api/repo-analysis",
    "clones / reads remote repos and calls the LLM"
   ],
   [
    "^/api/code-reviews",
    "calls the LLM / GitHub"
   ],
   [
    "^/api/review",
    "calls the LLM"
   ],
   [
    "^/api/conversations",
    "calls the LLM"
   ],
   [
    "^/(api/)?conversations",
    "calls the LLM"
   ],
   [
    "^/api/memory",
    "embeddings / LLM calls"
   ],
   [
    "^/api/ws/",
    "websocket upgrade paths"
   ]
  ],
  "_notes": "gitlark authenticates ONLY via GitHub OAuth (no password login, no test-account endpoint), so the fuzz runs UNAUTHENTICATED: authenticated routes answer 401 before their handlers run, so this covers public routes and the auth guard only (auth_loss_max 1.01 turns off the 'lost its auth' UNVERIFIED rule, a 401 wall is the normal state here). Reaching the authenticated surface needs a mintable throwaway token (a test-only login or a JWT signed with the dummy SECRET_KEY): documented follow-up, not guessed here."
 }
}
